 pass. A second machine rebases and stops when the repair is already on main.
 - **Every selected spec runs.** An affected gate runs the specs the watch map lists, a full gate every fast-tier spec, a slow gate only `z-nile/tests/slow.tsv`. Nothing is skipped because an earlier run passed. The same commit and the same change do the same work on any machine. The runner packs files by `<home>/.cache/spec-durations.tsv` (one line `<seconds>\t<path>`), a hint written after a run and safe to delete: with no file the run is ordered by path. `slow.tsv` is the committed list of specs those two gates skip, in the same line grammar; its seconds are not the live times.
 - **Watch miss**: a spec fails under `--full` but wasn't selected for the same diff. That's a hole in the map, a chore (z-ticket). `./zn watch-net` fills it and captures it, though it still types the capture a defect (d0353).
 
